  "context": "2026-11-03: the fetch-timing contract is decided in fetch-timing-contract-decision-20261103 and implemented by perf-arrow-aware-result-capture-20261030. Under the recommended option, full Arrow receipt (including draining streaming readers) stays inside the query timer and fetch_mode is recorded; Arrow-to-rows conversion for digests stays outside it. Re-read the recorded decision before starting; if the owner chose differently, update this item's acceptance. Origin: root-cause analysis of RF1 timing and its adversarial review.\n\nGuardrails (added 2026-11-03): no live-cloud runs (Databricks, Athena, BigQuery, Snowflake, ClickHouse Cloud, MotherDuck) without owner approval quoted in context; an adapter without a passing digest-parity run keeps rows as its default fetch; heavy runs only through make heavy-run or a lock-taking entry point; no explanatory comments in source (make comment-policy-check); changelog.d fragment required; re-read cited symbols before editing, since line numbers drift.\n\nLanded in batch arrow-result-fetch-2, narrowed to adapters that could run parity locally; cloud adapters (MotherDuck, Databricks, Athena, BigQuery incl. storage extra and uv.lock, Snowflake, ClickHouse Cloud) re-homed to perf-arrow-fetch-cloud-adapters-20261107. Parity evidence (rows vs arrow, TPC-H SF0.01, 22 queries, result digest and row count, via adapter.execute_query), logs and scripts under ~/Developer/benchmark_runs/arrow-parity/: DataFusion 22/22 identical, default arrow. GizmoSQL 22/22 identical against gizmodata/gizmosql:latest v1.42.2 run with mocker and torn down, default arrow. chDB 21/22 (chdb 3.7.2; the installed chdb 4.1.6 wheel does not load on this macOS): Q17 differs because the rows path returns NaN where the Arrow path returns NULL for an empty aggregate, so ClickHouse local stays on rows by default with fetch_mode=arrow opt-in. InfluxDB FlightSQL builds rows column-wise, no Arrow switch. Server ClickHouse has no Arrow path and stays on rows.",
  "description": "Replace fetchall/list() with Arrow paths in the current drivers (versions from uv.lock): DuckDB 1.5.5 duckdb.py:1049 and MotherDuck motherduck.py:222 — use to_arrow_table/to_arrow_reader (fetch_arrow_table is deprecated); Databricks databricks/adapter.py:2486 (fetchall_arrow); GizmoSQL gizmosql.py:1101 goes through base/sql_execution.py:84 fetchall — use fetch_arrow_table (wrapper at gizmosql.py:310 is only used for schema); Athena athena.py:961 (pyathena 3.36 ArrowCursor / as_arrow); ClickHouse Cloud clickhouse/client.py:257-269 (clickhouse-connect 1.8 query_arrow); chDB clickhouse/client.py:85-107 (keep pa.Table, skip to_pandas); InfluxDB influxdb/client.py:186-196 FlightSQL path only (per-cell as_py; the influxdb3 path at :166-177 is column-wise already). BigQuery bigquery.py:1561: to_arrow works but needs google-cloud-bigquery-storage (not locked) to beat REST; add the bqstorage extra. Snowflake snowflake.py:1323,1334: fetch_arrow_all is gated on the connector's pandas extra, which pins pandas<3 while the project needs pandas>=3 — verify it works or drop Snowflake from this item. Also cover CursorValidationQueryExecutionMixin (core/benchmark_mixins.py:182-189), which calls fetchall inside the timer for Presto/Trino, Redshift and Firebolt; those drivers have no Arrow path, so at minimum avoid double materialization.",
